Design decision: should signOut() unconditionally sign out from Google? If never initialized, calling `GoogleSignIn.instance.signOut()` on the real SDK without initialize... in 7.x, signOut() calls platform signOut which may throw if not initialized. My guard is right for the real world, but then after app restart with remembered session and sign-out without a fresh google sign-in, the Google SDK side session isn't cleared... but with remember-me restore, there was no active Google SDK session in this process anyway (the restore is from local storage). Signing out of Google SDK when we never signed in this process: nothing to clear. The plugin-side session persists across restarts on Android/iOS in the Google SDK itself. Hmm — for correctness, signOut() on a restored session SHOULD attempt google sign-out to fully disconnect the SDK session. With 7.x, calling signOut() without initialize() — the platform signOut on iOS/Android might handle uninitialized gracefully or throw.

Safer real-world approach: initialize() lazily in signOut() too:

```dart
Future<void> signOut() async {
 await _ensureGoogleInitialized();
 await _google.signOut();
}
``

